## Five scenarios candidates must be able to explain

Scenario 1: Cross-tenant access

A Hyderabad user tries to access a Bangalore task using its ID.

Expected explanation: The backend checks the authenticated user's membership and tenant authorization. It rejects the unauthorized request, regardless of the tenant ID supplied by the frontend.

Scenario 2: Simultaneous updates

Two users edit the same task.

Expected explanation: The backend uses version checking and rejects stale writes or invokes an explicit conflict-resolution strategy.

Scenario 3: Real-time updates

One user moves a task.

Expected explanation: The backend validates the request, commits the database change and broadcasts the resulting update to authorized users in the same tenant.

Scenario 4: Network disconnection

A user disconnects while another user modifies the board.

Expected explanation: On reconnection, the disconnected client reauthenticates, rejoins the authorized room and fetches the latest board state.

Scenario 5: Multiple organizations

A user has access to two organizations.

Expected explanation: The application retrieves the user's authorized memberships and only displays data belonging to the currently selected authorized organization and tenant.

